# Blender production

- Localize linked vendor materials before repairing alpha, normals, or color space.
- Build foliage as local Principled graphs. Do not depend on Botaniq addon node groups.
- Bark uses a cylindrical/longitudinal unwrap. Never object-project a 1:4 strip onto square-atlas UVs.
- Texture color spaces: albedo sRGB, data maps Non-Color.
- Keep bump/normal strength restrained. No emission used to hide bad albedo.
- Distance tiers: hero/foreground get real volume; EcoKit cards stay only where the camera cannot read their defects.
- Factory-startup local Blender is the zero-paid proof path. Do not require a saved .blend as the only entry point.
- Vendor source .blend/.zip files are read-only. Duplicate or overlay; do not overwrite purchased archives.
